From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:14:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mfreadwrite: Encode what the sink writer is given, and
 finalize the file.

The sink writer handed the samples it was given straight to the stream
sink without running them through the stream's converter and encoder
("FIXME: call the encoder"), and Finalize() returned E_NOTIMPL, so an
MP4 written through it got raw frames and was never completed:
PowerPoint's "Create a Video" gave up after two seconds with an empty
file.  WriteSample() now feeds each sample through the converter and
the encoder and queues what comes out for the sink as it asks; markers
keep their place.  Finalize() drains the transforms, delivers the rest,
finalizes the media sink and shuts it down, and returns when the file
is complete, or calls OnFinalize with MF_SINK_WRITER_ASYNC_CALLBACK; a
second call is MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST.  The todo_wines of
test_sink_writer_sample_process and GetServiceForStream go away, and
PowerPoint writes a playable 640x360 H.264 video of the slides in three
seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

